 {
  "coord": "266:25",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "term",
  "note": "Source's 'sign the disgrace' (echoed by Michaud's 'signing the glory') became 'sign away the honor'.",
  "replacement": "\"Well then, go back to the army,\" he said, drawing himself up to his full height and addressing Michaud with a gracious and majestic gesture. \"Tell our brave men, and all my good subjects wherever you go, that when I have no soldier left I will put myself at the head of my beloved nobility and my good peasants, and use the last resources of my empire. It still has more to give me than my enemies suppose,\" said the Emperor, growing more and more animated. \"But if it should ever be ordained by Divine Providence,\" he went on, raising his fine eyes, shining with emotion, to heaven, \"that my dynasty cease to reign on the throne of my ancestors, then, when I have used up every means in my power, I will let my beard grow down to here\" (he pointed halfway down his chest) \"and go and eat potatoes with the poorest of my peasants, rather than sign the disgrace of my country and of my beloved people, whose sacrifices I know how to value.\""
 },
