 {
  "coord": "269:12",
  "verdict": "FAIL",
  "category": "reversal",
  "note": "'Vice versa' lost: 'told her the same about him' wrongly repeats what Mary said of Nicholas instead of what he said of her.",
  "replacement": "Princess Mary was in mourning and did not go out into society, and Nicholas did not think it right to call on her again. Still, the governor's wife went on with her matchmaking. She told Nicholas the flattering things Princess Mary said about him, and told Princess Mary the flattering things he said about her, and she insisted that he declare himself to Princess Mary. To that end she arranged a meeting between the young people at the bishop's house before Mass."
